{"id": "EUVD-2026-108723", "enisaUuid": "bcfa3deb-8394-3c6a-bcfe-7b51d497044b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/gic-v4: Don't advertise VLPIs if no ITS is probed\n\nWhen accidentally setting \u201ckvm-arm.vgic_v4_enable=1\u201d on a system that has\nno MSI controller device tree node and GICv4, it results a panic as\n\u201cgic_domain\u201d is NULL and the kernel attempts to access it.\n\n    Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000028\n    Mem abort info:\n      ESR = 0x0000000096000006\n\n    CPU: 1 UID: 0 PID: 295 Comm: lkvm-static Not tainted 7.1.0-rc4-ge3f15ad3970e #5 PREEMPT\n    Hardware name: linux,dummy-virt (DT)\n    pstate: 81402005 (Nzcv daif +PAN -UAO -TCO +DIT -SSBS BTYPE=--)\n    pc : __irq_domain_instantiate+0x1d4/0x578\n    lr : __irq_domain_instantiate+0x1cc/0x578\n\nSet vLPI support to false at init time if the host has no ITS, so it\npropagates properly to kvm_vgic_global_state.has_gicv4.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e4cae9f1472ba3c9fe87edee24074618b51f537", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2508b8855acc96abe69be73b41b672f1ef12516", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e79934064be85fc9a3a6434da857307d8b78e33d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4761493dd663443f7353c184e6fa16e1cb3ac5a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab233119a19716b8f33e73ea7e092e0eb353cfbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8a911b3b07baa0aeb3dbc4e16a4670bd21bed40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e61654fbc3bc5d07ec9fafe29f33e19b2b5d0fd5", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98877"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98877", "GHSA-32qr-g6m6-8v7x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f25cac3-82b7-393a-ac5b-f06d4961e568", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "1c8c92be-73d9-32c0-be8c-69b90f9f5f7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.53"}, {"id": "1ce4f20d-fb2e-36dc-9050-9e29d42a0a71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "20233eb2-b8c4-3e99-b54b-1533a6d6f2bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "2cf31c42-c711-3412-92fb-91c11677908c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4761493dd663443f7353c184e6fa16e1cb3ac5a1"}, {"id": "342b9d6f-e4af-3316-bcde-f17633dc00b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ab233119a19716b8f33e73ea7e092e0eb353cfbf"}, {"id": "417dd365-4dc9-380c-a29b-303882725644", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "56280ada-8e1e-3144-a9f4-ba274e14cdcf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "6b081511-6cf0-3dd0-8647-3fb3853bce7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3e4cae9f1472ba3c9fe87edee24074618b51f537"}, {"id": "7b7d68f0-29cf-397a-aa10-4e2cc484cfb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <5.10.271"}, {"id": "93d229c2-1a80-3e56-8c61-70046ed6292a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "94f57db2-4139-32a0-81bf-da6cec56ff73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c8a911b3b07baa0aeb3dbc4e16a4670bd21bed40"}, {"id": "b1da14ce-366d-34ea-8703-4b59b7b83e56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <a2508b8855acc96a